cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use coa-judicial-behavior in your research, please cite it and the studies whose methods it follows, as below."
type: software
title: "coa-judicial-behavior: Ideology, activism, partisanship, and independence scores of federal appellate judges from CourtListener opinions"
abstract: >-
  A Python package that computes the ideology, activism, partisanship, and
  independence scores and judging styles of the judges of the federal courts
  of appeals, following the methods of Corey Rayburn Yung's studies, from
  opinions that courtpy collects from CourtListener and codes, and adds them
  to every vote as variables for control and prediction.
authors:
  - given-names: Corey Rayburn
    family-names: Yung
    email: coreyrayburnyung@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6524-9956"
version: 0.0.1
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/WithPrecedent/coa_judicial_behavior"
url: "https://WithPrecedent.github.io/coa_judicial_behavior"
keywords:
  - courtlistener
  - courts of appeals
  - empirical legal studies
  - judicial activism
  - judicial behavior
  - judicial ideology
  - judicial independence
  - partisanship
